{"id": "DemUlTJRyhD", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Why does Shani Dev never look anyone in the eye? Because the ONE time he did… baby Ganesha's head flew off. 👀🐘\n\nYou know the story where Shiva cuts the boy's head at Parvati's door (Shiva Purana). The Brahma Vaivarta Purana tells it differently:\n\n🪔 Shani was lost in prayer to Krishna when his wife came to him. He never looked up, so she cursed him: whoever you look at will be destroyed. From that day he kept his eyes on his feet.\n🪔 When baby Ganesha was born, all the gods came to bless him. Shani kept his head down. Parvati asked why, heard about the curse, and insisted: just one look.\n🪔 He glanced from the corner of his left eye, and the baby's head flew to the heavens.\n🪔 Vishnu flew north on Garuda and brought back an elephant's head. That's how Bappa got his elephant head.\n🪔 Parvati cursed Shani to lose his limbs. The gods begged for him, and she softened it to a limp, forever.\n\nThat's why Shani's gaze is feared… and why he limps. 🙏\n\nPart 2 is coming: Shani Dev's mother was a SHADOW. Follow so you don't miss it.\n\n📚 Our 15K Family Deal: Rishi Katha Books 1–3 (Shailputri, Brahmacharini, Chandraghanta) for ₹350 instead of ₹500, only till 21 Oct midnight. Comment FAMILY and we'll DM you the deal, or tap the link in bio (rishikatha.com).\n\n💬 Is your name Ganesh, Vinayak or Gajanan? Comment it!\n🔖 Save this for the next time someone asks why Ganesha has an elephant head, and share it with the Shani bhakt in your family.\n\n#shanidev #shani #ganesha #ganpatibappa #bappa #lordganesha #parvati #vishnu #garuda #brahmavaivartapurana #hindumythology #indianmythology #mythologystories #rishikatha #kidsbooksindia", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792247355, "like_count": 65773, "comment_count": 629, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-2135090307170663a", "ext": "m4a", "t